== and what those two SAY, which is the whole point of them ==
no folder: no folder at /srv/projects/ghost
no path:   type a folder path into the name field, then press Open Folder
== a path as a PERSON types it ==
~             -> /home/u
~/dev/gdash   -> /home/u/dev/gdash
/abs/path     -> /abs/path
dev/gdash     -> /w/dev/gdash
~someone/x    -> /w/~someone/x
(empty)       -> []
~/x, no HOME  -> /w/~/x
rel, no cwd   -> rel
